librtprocess Bayer demosaicing
------------------------------

Source: https://github.com/CarVac/librtprocess
Commit: 9a858270acb2096e2e403d932760ee688fcac425
Archive SHA-256:
a85bac0d67fc08ceaf61a7deeedff5ffaf8edabcebeb9a59924df378efc800f6

The app statically links the AMaZE, DCB, AHD, HPHD, IGV, LMMSE, VNG4,
Fast, and border kernels. The code comes from RawTherapee and its
contributors. License: GPL version 3 or later (LIBRTPROCESS_LICENSE.txt).
DCB demosaicing is by Jacek Gozdz (cuniek@kft.umcs.lublin.pl).
Its BSD notice is in DCB_LICENSE.txt.

scripts/prepare-rtprocess.mjs verifies the archive and applies counted
patches. The patches make the kernels stop on cancellation, split serial
HPHD passes into strips, and prevent an AMaZE tail write past a row.
Each changed source has a dated modification notice. The kernels run
without OpenMP. The adapter uses float input and output, and replaces the
outer bands of DCB, IGV, and LMMSE with the library's border interpolation
to correct edge artifacts. No integer quantization is used.

RawTherapee EAHD
----------------

Source: https://github.com/RawTherapee/RawTherapee
Version: 5.13, commit 1924179107995b01b73cdc7f4fe91e44fc8227a7
rtengine/eahd_demosaic.cc SHA-256:
d8bbe5fbdbab0932057f99de81eae14f09eb4be09141a930aef866e9e4aae4cc

Copyright (c) 2004-2018 Gabor Horvath and RawTherapee contributors.
Compilation unit and speed improvements: Ingo Weyrich, 2018.
License: GPL version 3 or later (LIBRTPROCESS_LICENSE.txt).

src/eahd.cpp ports EAHD and interpolate_row_rb_mul_pp from
rtengine/rawimagesource_i.h to the library interface. It keeps float green
values, computes CIELab directly, corrects the camera-matrix orientation,
fills the first and last rows, and stops on cancellation. The source header
lists these changes and retains the upstream copyright and license notice.
